{"meta":{"format_version":"5.0","model_format":"free","box_uv":false},"name":"rampart_earth","model_identifier":"rampart_earth","visible_box":[1,1,0],"variable_placeholders":"","multi_file_ruleset":"","variable_placeholder_buttons":[],"timeline_setups":[],"unhandled_root_fields":{"description":"# rampart_earth\n\nEarth rampart (Patch 5): a chunk of rammed earth built in layers of slightly different earth tones, with a battered (stepped-back) front face held by wooden stakes, a sod cap with grass tufts on top and a few stones in the face. Players line chunks up into an earthen wall; it is the only thing built from earth.\n\n- Footprint: 2 x 2 columns (32 x 32 units, 0.90 x 0.90 m; the notes ask for 1 m, rounded to whole columns), centred on the origin, front (enemy side) faces -Z. Height 71 u (2 m) to the sod.\n- Texture: 256 x 128, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering, flat pixel-art tones per material.\n- Cubes: finished 36, construction_0 22, construction_33 26, construction_66 34, ruined 33 (the state sets are cut from the finished cubes and map into the texture regions of the faces they were cut from).\n- The ends (+X and -X) are flat and full height so chunks placed side by side join into one continuous rampart.\n\n## State group sets (children of `root`; show exactly one)\n\n- `finished`: the finished building (visible by default).\n- `construction_0`, `construction_33`, `construction_66`: build progress at 0 %, 33 % and 66 % (staked outline and footing with materials waiting, then walls rising inside scaffold).\n- `ruined`: broken walls at uneven heights, rubble and fallen beams.\n- `rampart_earth_damaged.png`: damaged texture (cracks, scorch) for the same UVs; works on every group set.\n\n## Hit box\n\n- 32 x 71 x 32 centred at the origin (the damaged states keep the same hit box: the damage is visual)\n\n## Attachment points (empty groups)\n\n- `slot_wall_walk` at (0, 71, 2): where a defender stands on top."},"resolution":{"width":256,"height":128},"elements":[{"name":"earth_layer_1_a#6f4f32","box_uv":false,"render_order":"default","locked":false,"export":true,"scope":0,"allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[-16,0,-16],"to":[2,12,16],"autouv":0,"color":6,"origin":[-16,0,-16],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[200,60,218,72],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[202,32,234,44],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[218,60,236,72],"texture":0},"west":{"uv":[0,60,32,72],"texture":0},"up":{"uv":[0,0,18,32],"texture":0},"down":{"uv":[18,0,36,32],"texture":0}},"type":"cube","uuid":"5da0d5cb-98ab-4531-828f-dbb2f7c5b20b"},{"name":"earth_layer_1_b#7a5737","box_uv":false,"render_order":"default","locked":false,"export":true,"scope":0,"allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[2,0,-15.4],"to":[16,12,16],"autouv":0,"color":7,"origin":[2,0,-15.4],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[18,72,32,84],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[32,60,63,72],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[32,72,46,84],"texture":0},"west":{"uv":[63,60,94,72],"texture":0},"up":{"uv":[72,0,86,31],"texture":0},"down":{"uv":[86,0,100,31],"texture":0}},"type":"cube","uuid":"f01ed96d-c7b8-9ae3-f84f-c4521359998d"},{"name":"earth_layer_2_a#7a5737","box_uv":false,"render_order":"default","locked":false,"export":true,"scope":0,"allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[-16,12,-15],"to":[2,23,16],"autouv":0,"color":3,"origin":[-16,12,-15],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[27,95,45,106],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[74,72,105,83],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[45,95,63,106],"texture":0},"west":{"uv":[105,72,136,83],"texture":0},"up":{"uv":[36,0,54,31],"texture":0},"down":{"uv":[54,0,72,31],"texture":0}},"type":"cube","uuid":"f2ebf205-8a84-cbca-8546-5a801a36798d"},{"name":"earth_layer_2_b#644529","box_uv":false,"render_order":"default","locked":false,"export":true,"scope":0,"allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[2,12,-14.4],"to":[16,23,16],"autouv":0,"color":2,"origin":[2,12,-14.4],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[171,95,185,106],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[136,72,166,83],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[185,95,199,106],"texture":0},"west":{"uv":[166,72,196,83],"textu