1732844f7","f90f7358-a96e-bcba-674e-6f350c0e8239","5ad4f6d1-2730-39a5-71b1-477a7a472a73","a83bc05d-98f4-c9d1-29d7-f04d957d9108","0af5b09c-4f08-238f-d221-fb7946126953","78ff4ff2-4bff-3ef6-c1da-07c5969e0398","50010c40-1f97-17e6-a817-b2b566b13521","dff869fa-8997-7b97-fa14-81d51115e285","b3baf046-e10f-8392-90cb-fe5f11a8b043","c31450f2-e184-5ecf-05e2-8bd7f57cad10","2cf72116-7e93-f062-dae7-9345a84a234c","8315ef1f-9750-6ecc-855b-5c11d04c6b5b"],"reset":false,"shade":true,"mirror_uv":false,"autouv":0,"isOpen":false,"primary_selected":false}],"reset":false,"shade":true,"mirror_uv":false,"autouv":0,"isOpen":false,"primary_selected":false}],"textures":[{"name":"rampart_earth.png","path":"","folder":"","namespace":"","id":"0","group":"","scope":0,"width":256,"height":128,"uv_width":256,"uv_height":128,"particle":false,"use_as_default":false,"layers_enabled":false,"sync_to_project":"","file_format":"png","render_mode":"default","render_sides":"auto","wrap_mode":"limited","pbr_channel":"color","fps":7,"frame_time":1,"frame_order_type":"loop","frame_order":"","frame_interpolate":false,"visible":true,"internal":true,"saved":true,"uuid":"11092266-913e-7145-5d35-e712721cb8fd","source":"data:image/png;base64,","relative_path":""}],"description":"# rampart_earth\n\nEarth rampart (Patch 5): a chunk of rammed earth built in layers of slightly different earth tones, with a battered (stepped-back) front face held by wooden stakes, a sod cap with grass tufts on top and a few stones in the face. Players line chunks up into an earthen wall; it is the only thing built from earth.\n\n- Footprint: 2 x 2 columns (32 x 32 units, 0.90 x 0.90 m; the notes ask for 1 m, rounded to whole columns), centred on the origin, front (enemy side) faces -Z. Height 71 u (2 m) to the sod.\n- Texture: 256 x 128, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering, flat pixel-art tones per material.\n- Cubes: finished 36, construction_0 22, construction_33 26, construction_66 34, ruined 33 (the state sets are cut from the finished cubes and map into the texture regions of the faces they were cut from).\n- The ends (+X and -X) are flat and full height so chunks placed side by side join into one continuous rampart.\n\n## State group sets (children of `root`; show exactly one)\n\n- `finished`: the finished building (visible by default).\n- `construction_0`, `construction_33`, `construction_66`: build progress at 0 %, 33 % and 66 % (staked outline and footing with materials waiting, then walls rising inside scaffold).\n- `ruined`: broken walls at uneven heights, rubble and fallen beams.\n- `rampart_earth_damaged.png`: damaged texture (cracks, scorch) for the same UVs; works on every group set.\n\n## Hit box\n\n- 32 x 71 x 32 centred at the origin (the damaged states keep the same hit box: the damage is visual)\n\n## Attachment points (empty groups)\n\n- `slot_wall_walk` at (0, 71, 2): where a defender stands on top."}